<h2>What a tradie CRM actually needs</h2>

<p>Most CRMs are built for office workers. People who sit at desks, stare at dashboards, and have meetings about meetings. That is not you. You need something you can run from your phone, between jobs, with dirty hands and five minutes to spare.</p>

<p>Here is what a CRM for tradies actually needs to do:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Missed call text-back.</strong> When you cannot answer, an automatic SMS goes out so the lead does not disappear. More on this below, because this one feature alone is worth the price of admission.</li>
  <li><strong>A job pipeline.</strong> A simple visual board that shows every job at every stage: Enquiry, Quoted, Booked, In Progress, Complete, Paid. One glance and you know exactly where everything stands.</li>
  <li><strong>Simple quoting from your phone.</strong> Send a professional-looking quote in two minutes flat, right from the cab of your ute. No laptop required.</li>
  <li><strong>Scheduling and calendar sync.</strong> Book jobs and see your week at a glance. No double-bookings. No forgetting where you are supposed to be on Thursday arvo.</li>
  <li><strong>Automated follow-ups on unsent quotes.</strong> If you quoted someone three days ago and they have not responded, the system nudges them for you. <a href="/blog/automate-follow-up">Automating your follow-up</a> turns "I forgot" into "it is already handled."</li>
  <li><strong>Review requests after job completion.</strong> The moment you mark a job as done, an SMS asks the client to leave a Google review. No awkward conversations. Just consistent, automatic requests.</li>
  <li><strong>Mobile-first design.</strong> If it does not work brilliantly on a phone, it is useless to a tradie. Full stop.</li>
</ul>

<p>You do not need fancy reporting dashboards or AI-powered analytics. You need something simple that stops jobs from falling through the cracks.</p>

<blockquote><p>The best CRM for a tradie is the one you will actually use. If it is complicated, you will not open it. If it is simple, it becomes part of your routine.</p></blockquote>

<h2>The missed call text-back (this one feature pays for itself)</h2>

<p>If you only take one thing from this entire article, let it be this. Set up missed call text-back.</p>

<p>Here is how it works. When a call comes in and you cannot answer, the system automatically sends an SMS to the caller within 60 seconds. Something like:</p>

<p><strong>"Hey, sorry I missed your call. I am on a job right now. Can I call you back within the hour?"</strong></p>

<p>That is it. One text message. And it completely changes the game.</p>

<p>Why? Because the customer now knows three things. One, you exist. Two, you are busy (which means you are in demand, which is a good look). Three, you are going to call them back. They are not going to call the next tradie on the list because you have already made contact.</p>

<p>Without that text, all they know is that you did not answer. And that feels the same as "this business does not care about my call." So they move on.</p>

<p>Tradies who set up missed call text-back consistently report winning back jobs they would have lost. Some estimate it saves them thousands of dollars a month. And it runs completely on autopilot. You do not have to do anything. The system handles it while you keep working.</p>

<p>If you want to build out a proper follow-up sequence beyond just that first text, our guide on <a href="/blog/customer-follow-up-system">creating a customer follow-up system</a> walks through the entire process step by step.</p>

