<h2>Getting started without the tech headache</h2>

<p>If you have read this far, you are probably thinking one of two things. Either "this sounds great, where do I sign up" or "this sounds like a lot of tech I do not have time for."</p>

<p>Fair enough. Here is the honest truth: setting up a CRM takes a few hours. Not days. Not weeks. A few hours on a quiet Sunday arvo and you are sorted. You import your existing contacts (even if that means typing in numbers from your phone), set up your pipeline stages, write one missed call text-back message, and create one automated review request.</p>

<p>That is your foundation. Everything else, the follow-up sequences, the SMS campaigns, the quoting templates, can come later. Start small, see the results, and build from there.</p>

<p>The tradies who do best with a CRM are not the most tech-savvy ones. They are the ones who commit to using it consistently. Open it every morning. Move your jobs through the pipeline. Let the automations do their thing. Within a month, you will wonder how you ever ran your business without it.</p>

